; SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
;
; ! WHY (4 November 2026, voce 85). Every build system passes -pthread to a
; program or library that uses threads (Meson for HarfBuzz, CMake, qmake for
; Qt), and -rdynamic to executables (CMake on "Linux"). The EX-OS driver
; refused both: "unrecognized command-line option '-pthread'". As on Linux
; (gcc/config/gnu-user.opt), they are driver options, and exos.h/exos64.h
; say what they do: -pthread defines _REENTRANT and links -lpthread (an
; empty archive: the threads are in the libc), -rdynamic exports the
; program's symbols to the libraries it loads (--export-dynamic).

pthread
Driver

rdynamic
Driver
